      "description": "Watch Sporting Charleroi II vs Union St. Gilloise highlights and goals from Jupiler Pro League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 7, 2026. In a match characterized by intense pace and high-octane offensive displays, Sporting Charleroi II and Lommel United squared off in an electric Jupiler Pro League fixture. The encounter, held on September 7, 2026, served as a true test of grit for both sides throughout the afternoon. A breathless first half The game began with high stakes, as Ondrej Kricfalusi and Mardochee Nzita both picked up yellow cards early on, signaling the physical intensity of the match. The deadlock was broken in unusual fashion in the 12th minute when Mohamed Kone inadvertently sent the ball into his own net. The response was clinical: in the 27th minute, Freddy Mbemba netted a goal following a precise assist from Kevin Van Den Kerkhof . The action remained relentless, with Patrick Pfluecke putting Lommel United ahead in the 41st minute via a Jakob Napoleon Romsaas assist, only for Adem Zorgane to level the score for Sporting Charleroi II just minutes later in the 44th, shortly before Louis Patris was cautioned. The second half push After the break, the momentum did not let up. In the 49th minute, Kamiel van de Perre converted a strike off an assist from Besfort Zeneli , which proved to be the final turning point of the match. The remainder of the second half featured a series of tactical substitutions as both benches looked for fresh legs to shift the balance. Despite sustained pressure from both teams until the referee blew the final whistle in the 90+3rd minute, the scoreline held firm, concluding a day of truly gripping football."
